hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16183","He said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad and Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Raitah wife of Abdullah, and she was a craftswoman, selling and giving charity, and she said to Abdullah one day: Thou and thy child have busied me, so I cannot give charity with you. So he said: I do not love, if there is no reward in that, that thou do. So they asked about that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Thine is the reward of what thou spent on them."
"16184","He said: Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Raitah wife of Abdullah ibn Masud and mother of his child, and she was a craftswoman with her hand. He said: And she spent on him and on his child from her craft. She said: So I said to Abdullah ibn Masud: Thou and thy child have busied me from charity, so I cannot give charity with you anything. So Abdullah said to her: By Allah, I do not love, if there is no reward in that, that thou do. So she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman of craft, I sell of it, and there is for me nor for my child nor for my husband maintenance other than it, and they have busied me from charity, so I cannot give charity anything. Is there for me reward in what I spend? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Spend on them, for thine in that is the reward of what thou spent on them."
